  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Tech Solutions has $437M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. New Tech Solutions has received 2,592 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $168K. Obligations fell 26.6% year over year, down from $595M in FY25. Historical obligations show FY21 at $478M, FY22 at $500M, FY23 at $561M, FY24 at $567M, and FY25 at $595M. Top buyers are led by the Department of Defense with $130M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $78.9M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $55.8M. Market concentration is high in Other Computer Related Services, which accounts for $385M of obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing represents $29.9M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing represents $11.9M. This profile shows a fiscal-year-to-date pullback in obligations alongside continued reliance on defense and DHS demand and heavy exposure to Other Computer Related Services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "New Tech Solutions obligated $437M in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 26.6% year over year, from FY25 obligations of $595M. Fiscal-year history shows a peak in FY25 at $595M and a decline into FY26 at $437M. Award volume remains significant with 2,592 awards and an average award of $168K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and markets for New Tech Solutions?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $130M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $78.9M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $55.8M. Other top buyers include the Department of Justice at $45.6M and the Department of State at $22M. Other Computer Related Services is the dominant market for New Tech Solutions at $385M, with Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $29.9M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $11.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
